When monitoring a workflow run for the operator, send a read-only subagent to review the worker's diff as soon as the freeze event arrives, with the challenge's P2s and merge risks as its checklist.

**Why:** on 2026-09-24, duel-core-001's two official reviewers approved code where a keyboard throw (J then K 1–2 frames apart) always became a jab and a whiffing strike cancelled a connecting throw. The handoff subagent found and reproduced both, and they were fixed in the follow-up feature duel-core-fixes. For world-sea, the subagent's read-only `git merge-tree` plus test run on the merged tree proved the parallel branches merged cleanly before either was approved.

**How to apply:** keep the subagent read-only (use `git show` and `git merge-tree`, never checkout). Put its findings into a follow-up feature rather than hand-editing reviewed code. After a review blocks, `repair` is refused, so use a follow-up feature; if the general reviewer never finished, restore the snapshot on the old base so the whole diff gets reviewed. See [[visible-claude-sessions]].
